    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.95,
    "rationale": "The undiluted samples from the final hours show optical saturation of the plate reader. When hours 15 and 18 aliquots are diluted 10-fold, both yield readings of ~0.52 OD600, whereas linear scaling would predict ~0.11 OD600 (10% of the undiluted 1.08-1.10 readings). This 4.8-4.9-fold deviation from linearity demonstrates that the reader's response becomes non-linear above ~0.1-0.2 OD600 due to optical saturation—the instrument cannot accurately measure high cell densities. Back-calculating from the 10x dilution readings: true OD ≈ 0.52 × 10 = 5.2. Therefore, the culture's actual biomass in the final hours (~5.2 equivalent OD) is approximately 4.8-5× higher than the undiluted readings (1.08-1.12) indicate. The culture did not plateau; it continued growing or accumulating biomass, but this was masked by optical saturation."
